{"thought": "기존 단일 파일 초안과 시험의 완성도를 확인한 뒤에만 안전하게 교체합니다.", "action": "recall", "args": {"mode": "read", "path": "ops/a2a_v16.py", "offset": 0, "limit": 8000}, "observation": "{\"ok\": true, \"result\": {\"ok\": true, \"text\": \"import json,re,statistics,time,math\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\nimport httpx\\nsrc=Path('ops/a2a_v11.py').read_text(encoding='utf8')\\nold=\\\"x['price']<math.ceil((int(u.get('cost',0))+210)*100/99)\\\"\\nassert old in src\\nsrc=src.replace(old,\\\"not loss_allowed(u,x['price'],a,kit)\\\")\\nb={};exec(compile(src,'ops/a2a_v11.py','exec'),b)\\nb['NOUNS'].update({'백미':['쌀','백미'],'현미':['현미'],'잡곡':['잡곡'],'가정용 건조기':['건조기'],'의류건조기':['건조기'],'건조기':['건조기'],'신선채소':['신선채소','채소','시금치','콩나물'],'제철 채소':['채소','시금치','콩나물'],'채소':['채소','시금치','콩나물'],'두유':['두유'],'돼지고기':['돼지고기','삼겹살','한돈'],'삼겹살':['삼겹살']})\\nb['ORDER']=sorted(b['NOUNS'],key=len,reverse=True)\\ndef loss_allowed(u,price,a,kit):\\n floor=math.ceil((int(u.get('cost',0))+210)*100/99)\\n if price>=floor:return True\\n try:\\n  rows=json.loads(b['checked_path'](a,'loss_path','loss_reservations.json',kit.testing).read_text(encoding='utf8'));day=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d',time.gmtime(time.time()+32400));cap=30000\\n  if kit.testing:cap=min(cap,int(a.get('loss_cap',30000)))\\n  else:\\n   try:cap=min(cap,int(json.loads(Path('owner_limits.json').read_text()).get('max_loss_per_day',30000)))\\n   except (OSError,ValueError,TypeError):pass\\n  rows=[r for r in rows if r.get('day')==day]\\n  return sum(int(r['loss']) for r in rows)<=max(0,cap) and any(r.get('active') and r.get('unit')==u.get('unit') and r.get('sku')==u.get('sku') and r.get('grade')==u.get('grade') and int(r.get('price',-1))==price and int(r.get('loss',0))>=floor-price for r in rows)\\n except Exception:return False\\nb['loss_allowed']=loss_allowed\\ndef run(a,kit):\\n try:\\n  result=b['run'](a,kit)\\n  if result.get('ok') is False:return result\\n  d=a.get('data') if isinstance(a.get('data'),dict) else {};text=str(a.get('text') or '')\\n  payment=any(k in d for k in ('payment_mandate','checkout_mandate','tx_hash','fee_tx_hash')) or bool(re.search(r'환불|파손|보증\\\\s*청구',text))\\n  if not payment:\\n   requests=b['wanted'](text);repl", "ts": 1795751945}
{"thought": "Decisions 응답 형식과 다품목 선택 방식을 확인합니다.", "action": "recall", "args": {"mode": "read", "path": "ops/llm_shim.py", "offset": 0, "limit": 8000}, "observation": "{\"ok\": true, \"result\": {\"ok\": true, \"text\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Local OpenAI-compatible shim between the Round 4 kit and the OpenAI API.\\n\\nWhy: the kit (scripts/round4/agent_kit.py, read-only) sends `max_tokens`, which OpenAI's reasoning models\\n(gpt-5.4 and later, including gpt-6.1-sol) reject with 400 \\\"use max_completion_tokens instead\\\". The kit lets\\nagent.json point llm.base anywhere, so this shim sits on 127.0.0.1 and:\\n  - renames max_tokens to max_completion_tokens, raised to SHIM_MAX_COMPLETION (reasoning tokens count against it;\\n    the kit's 4000 would often leave no room for the answer),\\n  - adds reasoning_effort from AGENT_REASONING_EFFORT when set,\\n  - forwards to OPENAI_BASE_URL with OPENAI_API_KEY,\\n  - appends token usage (never message content) to logs/llm-shim.jsonl,\\n  - stops spending at the owner's daily_tokens (owner_limits.json, set in the app) or SHIM_DAILY_TOKENS total tokens per local day (default 15,000,000, a safety net above the ~6-8M a day expected after the 11-26 sleep rules; 0 = no cap): past the cap it\\n    answers the kit itself with a sleep move (no API call), so the agent rests until the next day instead of\\n    retrying. Customers are still answered by the a2a_handler tool, which needs no model.\\n  - FORGE ESCALATION (11-27): when the answer's move is forge_tool (the agent writing a tool's code and test, ~3% of\\n    steps but the ones that break sales when wrong), the same request goes again to SHIM_FORGE_MODEL (default\\n    gpt-6.2-sol, reasoning SHIM_FORGE_EFFORT, default medium) and that answer is returned instead. The kit gives up on\\n    a socket silent for 60 s, so the second call gets what is left of SHIM_FORGE_DEADLINE (55 s); if it fails or runs\\n    out, the first answer stands. SHIM_FORGE_MODEL= (empty) turns this off.\\n  - DECISIONS (11-27): POST /v1/decisions is passed to OpenAI's Decisions API with the key added here, so a forged\\n    tool can ask typed questions (choice/predicate/score) on 127.0.0.", "ts": 1795751949}
